  "instructions": [
    "Preheat the oven to 425°F.",
    "Stir together the curry powder, paprika, cumin, salt, and pepper in a small bowl.",
    "Spread the cauliflower and chickpeas on separate baking sheets. Toss the chickpeas with 1 tbsp olive oil and 1 tbsp of the spice mix; toss the cauliflower with the remaining 2 tbsp oil and the rest of the spice mix.",
    "Roast both sheets for 30 minutes, shaking the chickpeas and tossing the cauliflower halfway through. Pull the chickpeas out at 30 minutes, then let the cauliflower roast 5-10 minutes longer, until lightly charred.",
    "Blend the cilantro, parsley, tahini, lemon juice, garlic, cumin, salt, and pepper. With the blender running, stream in the warm water and blend until smooth.",
    "Divide the rice between 4 bowls. Top with the roasted cauliflower and chickpeas, add cucumber and tomatoes if using, and drizzle with the Green Tahini Sauce."
